        "locale": "en",
        "title": "Choice",
        "takeaway": "Scarcity makes choice unavoidable; economics asks what guides a choice, which alternative is forgone, and who bears the consequences.",
        "definition": "Choice is the selection of one option, or a combination of options, from two or more feasible alternatives that cannot all be achieved under the available resource constraint.",
