    "content": {
      "zh-CN": {
        "id": "u1-07-equity",
        "locale": "zh-CN",
        "title": "公平",
        "takeaway": "公平判断结果或过程是否公正，它依赖价值标准，因此不能仅由市场数量或平均值决定。",
        "definition": "公平是关于经济资源、机会、负担和结果是否以公正方式分配的规范性概念；不同社会可能采用需要、贡献、机会或权利等标准。",
        "causalChain": [
          "识别资源、机会或负担的分配",
          "选择判断公正的标准",
          "比较不同群体受到的待遇与结果",
          "设计或评价改变分配的政策"
        ],
        "realWorldExample": {
          "title": "比较不平等与贫困政策",
          "sourceUrl": "https://www.oecd.org/en/topics/inequality-and-poverty.html",
          "observedAt": "2026-09-29",
          "explanation": "OECD 对收入不平等、贫困和社会流动的研究展示了税收与转移支付如何改变不同群体的可支配收入，也说明公平评价需要说明采用的标准。"
        },
        "misconceptions": [
          "公平不必意味着每个人获得完全相同的数量。",
          "声称一项政策更公平时，必须说明对谁、按什么原则更公平。"
        ],
        "examApplication": [
          "在评价段落中明确公平标准和受影响群体。",
          "讨论效率—公平权衡时不要假设两者必然冲突，应说明机制。"
        ],
        "summary": [
          "公平是一种规范性判断。",
          "公平标准可能包括需要、机会与贡献。",
          "公平分析必须识别群体和分配机制。"
        ],
        "explanation": "经济政策不仅改变总产出，也改变谁获得收入、服务和机会。公平分析把注意力放在这些分配上，并要求说明用什么原则判断结果。\n\n例如，按需要提供更多支持、按贡献给予回报和确保所有人拥有相同机会，都是可能的公平观。它们可能得出不同政策结论，因此答案应公开价值标准，而不是把“公平”当作无需解释的标签。"
      },
      "en": {
        "id": "u1-07-equity",
        "locale": "en",
        "title": "Equity",
        "takeaway": "Equity judges whether a process or outcome is fair; it depends on an explicit value standard rather than on market quantities or averages alone.",
        "definition": "Equity is a normative concept concerning the fairness of the distribution of economic resources, opportunities, burdens, and outcomes, assessed through principles such as need, contribution, opportunity, or rights.",
        "causalChain": [
          "Identify how resources, opportunities, or burdens are distributed",
          "Choose a principle of fairness",
          "Compare the treatment and outcomes of different groups",
          "Design or evaluate a policy that changes the distribution"
        ],
        "realWorldExample": {
          "title": "Comparing inequality and poverty policies",
          "sourceUrl": "https://www.oecd.org/en/topics/inequality-and-poverty.html",
          "observedAt": "2026-09-29",
          "explanation": "OECD work on inequality, poverty, and mobility shows how taxes and transfers alter disposable income across groups. It also demonstrates why an equity judgement must reveal the standard being applied."
        },
        "misconceptions": [
          "Equity need not mean that every person receives an identical amount.",
          "A claim that a policy is fairer is incomplete unless it specifies for whom and according to which principle."
        ],
        "examApplication": [
          "Name both the fairness criterion and the affected groups in an evaluation paragraph.",
          "Do not assume an efficiency-equity trade-off; explain the mechanism that creates or avoids one."
        ],
        "summary": [
          "Equity is a normative judgement.",
          "Need, opportunity, and contribution are possible standards.",
          "Equity analysis identifies groups and the distribution mechanism."
        ],
        "explanation": "Economic policy changes not only total output but also who receives income, services, and opportunities. Equity analysis concentrates on that distribution and requires a stated principle for judging it.\n\nSupport according to need, reward according to contribution, and equal access to opportunity are all plausible ideas of fairness. Because they can point toward different policies, a strong argument makes its value standard visible rather than treating equity as a self-explanatory label."
      }
    },
