    "content": {
      "zh-CN": {
        "id": "u1-14-opportunity-cost",
        "locale": "zh-CN",
        "title": "机会成本",
        "takeaway": "机会成本是作出选择时放弃的最佳可行替代方案的价值，而不是所有放弃选项之和。",
        "definition": "机会成本是在资源用于某项选择后无法获得的次优可行方案的收益或价值。",
        "causalChain": [
          "稀缺产生多个竞争用途",
          "按价值排列可行方案",
          "选择排名最高的方案",
          "排名第二且被放弃的方案构成机会成本"
        ],
        "realWorldExample": {
          "title": "公共预算的替代用途",
          "sourceUrl": "https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/FM",
          "observedAt": "2026-09-29",
          "explanation": "IMF《财政监测》讨论政府支出与财政空间。新增一项支出会占用资金和执行能力，其机会成本是同一资源原本可以支持的最佳替代政策。"
        },
        "misconceptions": [
          "机会成本不是所有被放弃方案的总和，只取最佳替代方案。",
          "沉没成本已经无法收回，不应与当前选择的机会成本混淆。"
        ],
        "examApplication": [
          "用“选择 A 的机会成本是放弃的最佳方案 B”完整表达。",
          "PPC 题中用另一种产品减少的数量衡量机会成本。"
        ],
        "summary": [
          "机会成本源于稀缺和选择。",
          "它只对应最佳被放弃方案。",
          "成本可用金钱、时间、产出或福祉表示。"
        ],
        "explanation": "选择一个用途意味着同一资源不能同时完整用于其他用途。经济学把最有价值的被放弃方案称为机会成本，以此显示决策的真实取舍。\n\n机会成本取决于当时可行的方案和决策者的目标，所以并非固定金额。它可以是失去的收入、时间、产出或环境质量。若替代方案不可行，就不应计入机会成本。"
      },
      "en": {
        "id": "u1-14-opportunity-cost",
        "locale": "en",
        "title": "Opportunity cost",
        "takeaway": "Opportunity cost is the value of the best feasible alternative forgone when a choice is made, not the sum of every rejected option.",
        "definition": "Opportunity cost is the benefit or value of the next-best feasible alternative that cannot be obtained once resources are committed to a chosen use.",
        "causalChain": [
          "Scarcity creates competing uses",
          "Feasible alternatives are ranked by value",
          "The highest-ranked option is selected",
          "The second-ranked forgone option is the opportunity cost"
        ],
        "realWorldExample": {
          "title": "Alternative uses of a public budget",
          "sourceUrl": "https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/FM",
          "observedAt": "2026-09-29",
          "explanation": "The IMF Fiscal Monitor discusses government spending and fiscal space. A new programme uses finance and administrative capacity; its opportunity cost is the best alternative policy that those resources could have supported."
        },
        "misconceptions": [
          "Opportunity cost is not the total of all forgone options; it is the best one.",
          "A sunk cost that cannot be recovered is not the opportunity cost of a decision made now."
        ],
        "examApplication": [
          "Use the complete statement: the opportunity cost of choosing A is the best forgone alternative B.",
          "On a PPC, measure the cost by the reduction in output of the other good."
        ],
        "summary": [
          "Opportunity cost follows from scarcity and choice.",
          "Only the best forgone alternative counts.",
          "Cost may be expressed in money, time, output, or well-being."
        ],
        "explanation": "Selecting one use prevents the same resource from being devoted fully to another. Economics calls the most valuable rejected option the opportunity cost, making the true trade-off in a decision visible.\n\nThe cost depends on the feasible alternatives and the decision-maker's objectives at that moment, so it is not a fixed cash amount. It can take the form of lost income, time, output, or environmental quality. An impossible alternative should not be counted."
      }
    },
