    "content": {
      "zh-CN": {
        "id": "u1-24-economic-models",
        "locale": "zh-CN",
        "title": "经济模型的作用与局限",
        "takeaway": "经济模型有意简化现实来突出关键关系；好模型不是细节最多，而是在明确假设下对问题有解释力。",
        "definition": "经济模型是对现实经济主体、约束和关系的有目的简化，用文字、图形或数学表达因果机制并形成可检验预测。",
        "causalChain": [
          "研究者提出一个具体问题",
          "保留被认为关键的变量和关系",
          "用假设隔离机制并推出预测",
          "把预测与证据比较后修正模型"
        ],
        "realWorldExample": {
          "title": "中央银行用模型解释政策传导",
          "sourceUrl": "https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/education/education-resources",
          "observedAt": "2026-09-29",
          "explanation": "英格兰银行的教育资料把利率、消费、投资、产出和通胀组织为简化关系。模型帮助解释传导方向，但真实效果仍取决于预期、金融状况和时滞。"
        },
        "misconceptions": [
          "模型不现实的某个细节不一定使模型无用；关键是简化是否破坏所研究的机制。",
          "模型结论是有条件的预测，不是任何时间地点都成立的保证。"
        ],
        "examApplication": [
          "使用图形前先写出关键假设，并在评价时放松其中一个假设。",
          "说明模型能解释什么，也说明它遗漏了哪些相关变量或群体。"
        ],
        "summary": [
          "模型把复杂现实压缩成关键关系。",
          "假设决定结论的适用范围。",
          "预测需要证据检验和迭代。"
        ],
        "explanation": "现实经济包含太多同时变化的因素，无法一次全部分析。模型通过选择变量、设定假设和表达关系，使一个机制变得可理解。PPC、供需图和 AD–AS 都属于模型。\n\n简化带来力量也带来局限。若遗漏因素与问题无关，模型仍可有效；若遗漏因素改变结论方向，模型就需要扩展。经济学家会比较预测和证据，而不是把模型当作现实的缩小照片。"
      },
      "en": {
        "id": "u1-24-economic-models",
        "locale": "en",
        "title": "Purposes and limits of economic models",
        "takeaway": "An economic model deliberately simplifies reality to isolate important relationships; the best model is useful for a question under clear assumptions, not the one with the most detail.",
        "definition": "An economic model is a purposeful simplification of agents, constraints, and relationships, expressed verbally, graphically, or mathematically to explain a mechanism and generate testable predictions.",
        "causalChain": [
          "A researcher specifies a focused question",
          "Variables and relationships judged essential are retained",
          "Assumptions isolate a mechanism and yield predictions",
          "Predictions are compared with evidence and the model is revised"
        ],
        "realWorldExample": {
          "title": "A central bank models policy transmission",
          "sourceUrl": "https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/education/education-resources",
          "observedAt": "2026-09-29",
          "explanation": "Bank of England education resources organise interest rates, consumption, investment, output, and inflation into simplified relationships. The model clarifies transmission while expectations, financial conditions, and lags shape the actual effect."
        },
        "misconceptions": [
          "An unrealistic detail does not automatically make a model useless; the test is whether the simplification damages the mechanism being studied.",
          "A model conclusion is a conditional prediction, not a guarantee for every time and place."
        ],
        "examApplication": [
          "State key assumptions before using a diagram, then relax one assumption in evaluation.",
          "Explain both what the model illuminates and which relevant variables or groups it omits."
        ],
        "summary": [
          "Models compress complexity into selected relationships.",
          "Assumptions define the range of a conclusion.",
          "Predictions must face evidence and revision."
        ],
        "explanation": "An economy contains too many changing elements to analyse simultaneously. A model selects variables, sets assumptions, and expresses relationships so that one mechanism becomes intelligible. The PPC, supply and demand, and AD–AS are all models.\n\nSimplification is both the source of power and a limitation. Omitting an irrelevant detail may be harmless; omitting a factor that changes the direction of a result is not. Economists confront predictions with evidence rather than treating a model as a miniature photograph of reality."
      }
    },
