        "title": "Normative economics and value judgements",
        "takeaway": "Normative economics asks how the economy ought to be; facts reveal consequences but cannot alone decide which values deserve priority.",
        "definition": "Normative economics evaluates policies, institutions, or outcomes as desirable, better, or required by applying value standards such as equity, freedom, efficiency, sustainability, or well-being.",
