        "id": "u1-35-equality-equity",
        "locale": "en",
        "title": "Equality and equity",
        "takeaway": "Equality describes identical or less dispersed distributions, while equity judges whether a distribution is fair; the two may overlap or equity may require different treatment.",
        "definition": "Equality is a condition of sameness or smaller differences in resources, opportunities, or outcomes. Equity evaluates whether treatment and distribution are justified by an explicit principle of fairness.",
