        "takeaway": "A circular economy treats the economy, society, and environment as interdependent systems and replaces take-make-dispose with lower material use, longer use, and retained value.",
        "definition": "A circular economy is a framework for designing and organising production and consumption to reduce extraction and waste, retain value in products, components, and materials, and support regeneration of natural systems.",
